  "question_stem": "A particle, $P$, travels in a straight line, starting from a point $O$ with velocity $6 \\mathrm{m s}^{-1}$. The acceleration of $P$ at time $t$ s after leaving $O$ is $a \\mathrm{m s}^{-2}$, where $$a = -1.5t^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\quad \\text{for } 0 \\le t \\le 1,$$ $$a = 1.5t^{\\frac{1}{2}} - 3t^{-\\frac{1}{2}} \\quad \\text{for } t > 1.$$",
  "context_texts": [
    "$v(1)=5\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$ to determine the integration constant.",
    "For $t>1$, use $v=\\frac38t^4-6\\sqrt t+10$"
  ],
